(7116621, 1086340, 30861, '<td valign="top">Well, that''s an amusing take :-) You''ve got the Kraken, you''ve got a sophisticated dive-suit to fill in for the submarine. The camera cracks me up. The whole thing''s processed nicely. As an aside, that''s the biggest silver dollar fish I''ve ever seen if it''s the same size as a giant squid :-)<br/> <br/>6 from me.</td>', 'Well, that''s an amusing take :-) You''ve got the Kraken, you''ve got a sophisticated dive-suit to fill in for the submarine. The camera cracks me up. The whole thing''s processed nicely. As an aside, that''s the biggest silver dollar fish I''ve ever seen if it''s the same size as a giant squid :-) 6 from me.', '2013-10-16 15:58:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116627, 1086453, 153814, '<td valign="top">Wow what a cool shot.<br/>It looks like an abstract skull.</td>', 'Wow what a cool shot.It looks like an abstract skull.', '2013-10-16 16:00:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116628, 1087125, 30861, '<td valign="top">This, for me, is just a snapshot taken with no concern for the quality of the light, and then not processed to advantage at all. Plus the pond''s not golden at all. You really need the golden-hour light to make this one work for you.<br/> <br/>4 from me.</td>', 'This, for me, is just a snapshot taken with no concern for the quality of the light, and then not processed to advantage at all. Plus the pond''s not golden at all. You really need the golden-hour light to make this one work for you. 4 from me.', '2013-10-16 16:00:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116636, 1087141, 30861, '<td valign="top">A striking image of remarkably intense clarity, presumably infrared though, if so, a nicely muted infrared. Technically it''s excellent. I wonder if you need all the space on the left, but it''s a nit. As far as fitting the book, it does so very well. Good job capturing the intensity of the religious theme that ties the book together.<br/> <br/>8 from me, with the possibility of moving up at voting''s end.</td>', 'A striking image of remarkably intense clarity, presumably infrared though, if so, a nicely muted infrared. Technically it''s excellent. I wonder if you need all the space on the left, but it''s a nit. As far as fitting the book, it does so very well. Good job capturing the intensity of the religious theme that ties the book together. 8 from me, with the possibility of moving up at voting''s end.', '2013-10-16 16:10:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116637, 1087122, 124815, '<td valign="top">One of the most literal illustration of the title of a masterpiece that does not send me one bit to think of the novel.<br/>The sharpening is way to pronounced, the foreground is unnecessarily blurry. I feel that you have to take the picture again to give justice to this place<br/>4</td>', 'One of the most literal illustration of the title of a masterpiece that does not send me one bit to think of the novel.The sharpening is way to pronounced, the foreground is unnecessarily blurry. I feel that you have to take the picture again to give justice to this place4', '2013-10-16 16:14:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116638, 1086979, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is a remarkably lovely image but it has absolutely nothing to do with the novel. The novel is a dystopian vision of the near future, a bleak, industrial future marked by conformity and despair, it''s all about people and their struggles. THIS is a romantic vision, not a dystopian one. For what it''s worth, the novel''s title borrows from Shakespeare: "O, brave new world, that has such people in it!"<br/> <br/>It''s a good picture, 5 would make it below average which I don''t want to do, so I give it a 6.</td>', 'This is a remarkably lovely image but it has absolutely nothing to do with the novel. The novel is a dystopian vision of the near future, a bleak, industrial future marked by conformity and despair, it''s all about people and their struggles. THIS is a romantic vision, not a dystopian one. For what it''s worth, the novel''s title borrows from Shakespeare: "O, brave new world, that has such people in it!" It''s a good picture, 5 would make it below average which I don''t want to do, so I give it a 6.', '2013-10-16 16:15:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116639, 1086700, 109387, '<td valign="top">One of my favorite short stories/novels. It works to tell the story but I don''t know if voters will get it - this is DPC ;)</td>', 'One of my favorite short stories/novels. It works to tell the story but I don''t know if voters will get it - this is DPC ;)', '2013-10-16 16:15:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116640, 1086734, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is gorgeous! Where the heck are you? Wonderful drama and processing.<br/> <br/>Works well with the book, which not only takes PLACE in the Alps (Davos, if I recall correctly) but use the METAPHOR of mountains at several levels as it wends its elusive way towards a conclusion. <br/> <br/>Well done, an 8 for now (I sort my highest votes up when I am done)</td>', 'This is gorgeous! Where the heck are you? Wonderful drama and processing. Works well with the book, which not only takes PLACE in the Alps (Davos, if I recall correctly) but use the METAPHOR of mountains at several levels as it wends its elusive way towards a conclusion.  Well done, an 8 for now (I sort my highest votes up when I am done)', '2013-10-16 16:19:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116643, 1086865, 153814, '<td valign="top">Beautiful landscape with very nice colors it''s just a tad dark.<br/>The snows of Kilimanjaro is more of a short story not a classic novel.<br/>Still nicely done.</td>', 'Beautiful landscape with very nice colors it''s just a tad dark.The snows of Kilimanjaro is more of a short story not a classic novel.Still nicely done.', '2013-10-16 16:22:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116644, 1086692, 153814, '<td valign="top">Nice take on the challenge.</td>', 'Nice take on the challenge.', '2013-10-16 16:23:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116651, 1086744, 103142, '<td valign="top">I love all the dew drops on this. I can''t tell if this is a bit soft or not. (I''ve been having problems with my eyes, so it might be me.) I do wish there was more detail in Charlotte, though. She seems dark. I''m wondering if she was lightened, if we could see more details. :)<br/> <br/>Nice find!</td>', 'I love all the dew drops on this. I can''t tell if this is a bit soft or not. (I''ve been having problems with my eyes, so it might be me.) I do wish there was more detail in Charlotte, though. She seems dark. I''m wondering if she was lightened, if we could see more details. :) Nice find!', '2013-10-16 16:48:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116652, 1086939, 103142, '<td valign="top">Very nice. I like the swirls in the clouds and the color palette. I also like the silhouette in the front. -7-</td>', 'Very nice. I like the swirls in the clouds and the color palette. I also like the silhouette in the front. -7-', '2013-10-16 16:49:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116654, 1087222, 109387, '<td valign="top">The idea could be ok, but what happened during the editing? Skin and clothes have almost lost their shapes.</td>', 'The idea could be ok, but what happened during the editing? Skin and clothes have almost lost their shapes.', '2013-10-16 16:49:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116657, 1087207, 103142, '<td valign="top">Had to search to get the reference. The cabbage is quite nice, but something doesn''t feel right with the composition. I think it would have worked better if the kings were tucked under the cabbage more? Right now they seem too separated for the kings to be that soft. The eye sees it as two different subjects, one out of focus, instead of one composition with a shallow dof (at least that''s how my eye is seeing it :) Plus the cards are bright next to the gorgeous lighting of the cabbage, it just keeps drawing the eye to something not as interesting. -5-</td>', 'Had to search to get the reference. The cabbage is quite nice, but something doesn''t feel right with the composition. I think it would have worked better if the kings were tucked under the cabbage more? Right now they seem too separated for the kings to be that soft. The eye sees it as two different subjects, one out of focus, instead of one composition with a shallow dof (at least that''s how my eye is seeing it :) Plus the cards are bright next to the gorgeous lighting of the cabbage, it just keeps drawing the eye to something not as interesting. -5-', '2013-10-16 16:58:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116659, 1087198, 109387, '<td valign="top">Beautiful portrait, it can do well IMO.</td>', 'Beautiful portrait, it can do well IMO.', '2013-10-16 17:01:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116662, 1086858, 147247, '<td valign="top">Agra Fort, right? Love the photo!</td>', 'Agra Fort, right? Love the photo!', '2013-10-16 17:10:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116664, 1086858, 30861, '<td valign="top">I love the delicacy of the rendering here, the frieze-like quality of the processing, which perfectly presents the elaborate intricacy of both materials and architecture. On a further technical note, you''ve squared it up nearly flawlessly; there''s a bit of keystoning (slightly wider at top than at bottom, but the horizontals seem spot on, the POV is exactly on center, it''s all as it should be.<br/> <br/>Fits the book fine too. One might have expected a more decadent picture, but....<br/> <br/>Regardless. It''s an 8 for now, with possible bump depending on the rest of my voting.</td>', 'I love the delicacy of the rendering here, the frieze-like quality of the processing, which perfectly presents the elaborate intricacy of both materials and architecture. On a further technical note, you''ve squared it up nearly flawlessly; there''s a bit of keystoning (slightly wider at top than at bottom, but the horizontals seem spot on, the POV is exactly on center, it''s all as it should be. Fits the book fine too. One might have expected a more decadent picture, but.... Regardless. It''s an 8 for now, with possible bump depending on the rest of my voting.', '2013-10-16 17:17:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116669, 1087135, 30861, '<td valign="top">The Bell Jar is a novel about madness, emptiness, and pain. There''s a sense in which the pain can be seen to lead to rebirth, and a butterfly, emerged from its chrysalis, can be seen to embody that transformation, so the connection to the novel''s not that far-fetched. Notwithstanding that, however, this is an awfully cheerful image to represent such a bleak book.<br/> <br/>Also, as a nit, this isn''t shaped like any bell jar I''VE ever seen. Bell jars are designed to seal an atmosphere or a vacuum, and they are usually shaped like cylindrical domes.<br/> <br/>Still, it''s got a deeper-than-obvious connection to the book and it''s competently crafted. I''ll give it a 6.</td>', 'The Bell Jar is a novel about madness, emptiness, and pain. There''s a sense in which the pain can be seen to lead to rebirth, and a butterfly, emerged from its chrysalis, can be seen to embody that transformation, so the connection to the novel''s not that far-fetched. Notwithstanding that, however, this is an awfully cheerful image to represent such a bleak book. Also, as a nit, this isn''t shaped like any bell jar I''VE ever seen. Bell jars are designed to seal an atmosphere or a vacuum, and they are usually shaped like cylindrical domes. Still, it''s got a deeper-than-obvious connection to the book and it''s competently crafted. I''ll give it a 6.', '2013-10-16 17:32:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116683, 1086987, 50695, '<td valign="top">A pretty semi-abstract image. A competent version of something I''ve seen before. I haven''t read the book but at least there''s a connection with the title. 5</td>', 'A pretty semi-abstract image. A competent version of something I''ve seen before. I haven''t read the book but at least there''s a connection with the title. 5', '2013-10-16 18:15:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116684, 1086105, 50695, '<td valign="top">This does hold some of the menace of the aliens from that book, thanks to the ominous red over the green, and the high, hulking platform. The composition is okay. 5</td>', 'This does hold some of the menace of the aliens from that book, thanks to the ominous red over the green, and the high, hulking platform. The composition is okay. 5', '2013-10-16 18:17:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116685, 1086340, 50695, '<td valign="top">This is a picture of a fish tank, focusing on the props more than the fish. The props are appropriate to your title, but it''s one of those shots that has no life beyond the challenge. 3</td>', 'This is a picture of a fish tank, focusing on the props more than the fish. The props are appropriate to your title, but it''s one of those shots that has no life beyond the challenge. 3', '2013-10-16 18:18:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116689, 1087190, 50695, '<td valign="top">Negatives: yet another shot of something on fire with a black background. yet another shot of burning paper taken for this book.<br/> <br/>Positives: you''re burning John Grisham even though the title is Ray Bradbury. That''s hilarious to me. Plus, the scattered pages go outside the frame, making for a more interesting composition. <br/> <br/>End result: 4</td>', 'Negatives: yet another shot of something on fire with a black background. yet another shot of burning paper taken for this book. Positives: you''re burning John Grisham even though the title is Ray Bradbury. That''s hilarious to me. Plus, the scattered pages go outside the frame, making for a more interesting composition.  End result: 4', '2013-10-16 18:20:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116691, 1087184, 50695, '<td valign="top">Not a very imaginative or interesting shot, but I do like the honesty of just seeing someone perform his job, and he seems like an interesting character. Also, the bright greens and blues are nice. 5</td>', 'Not a very imaginative or interesting shot, but I do like the honesty of just seeing someone perform his job, and he seems like an interesting character. Also, the bright greens and blues are nice. 5', '2013-10-16 18:22:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116693, 1086433, 50695, '<td valign="top">I like how you''ve evoked the feeling of a robot simply by showing something mechanical with an "eye". The contre jour helps with this effect. Nice light. 6</td>', 'I like how you''ve evoked the feeling of a robot simply by showing something mechanical with an "eye". The contre jour helps with this effect. Nice light. 6', '2013-10-16 18:23:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116694, 1087198, 50695, '<td valign="top">In general, I''m not a big fan of portraits that are cropped this close. It''s too hard to get a sense of a person this way. Sometimes it''s pulled off, but not in this case. The background elements are distracting. 4</td>', 'In general, I''m not a big fan of portraits that are cropped this close. It''s too hard to get a sense of a person this way. Sometimes it''s pulled off, but not in this case. The background elements are distracting. 4', '2013-10-16 18:24:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116695, 1087096, 50695, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous light and texture. Well composed between shaded areas and lit areas, with the placement of your two subjects. Much too joyful for the book, but I give you a 7 for a great shot.</td>', 'Gorgeous light and texture. Well composed between shaded areas and lit areas, with the placement of your two subjects. Much too joyful for the book, but I give you a 7 for a great shot.', '2013-10-16 18:26:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116696, 1087001, 50695, '<td valign="top">A competent macro shot of a spider, but nothing to hold my interest. 3</td>', 'A competent macro shot of a spider, but nothing to hold my interest. 3', '2013-10-16 18:27:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116706, 1086767, 124982, '<td valign="top">Voted earlier, coming back to comment:<br/> <br/>Simple splendid take on the challenge. Very eerie and appropriate. Just love this. Top score for the challenge for me!</td>', 'Voted earlier, coming back to comment: Simple splendid take on the challenge. Very eerie and appropriate. Just love this. Top score for the challenge for me!', '2013-10-16 19:47:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116707, 1087135, 124982, '<td valign="top">Quite beautiful in the sharpness and clarity. Wish the crop was a lot tighter, but that''s just my preference. Lovely image, top 3 for me.</td>', 'Quite beautiful in the sharpness and clarity. Wish the crop was a lot tighter, but that''s just my preference. Lovely image, top 3 for me.', '2013-10-16 19:48:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116708, 1087219, 124815, '<td valign="top">I remember that the idea of  the Black Swan event depends on the observer.<br/>This being said, I believe that you mostly illustrated the title.<br/>What I believe is a flaw here is the lack of a certain mathematical/geometrical meaning to your image: the cropping of the beautiful head of the swan seems random, more cropping might have had more impact or the entire graceful curve would have made it even better. There are more variables such as the grey triangle on the upper left corner, the indecisive composition.<br/>6</td>', 'I remember that the idea of  the Black Swan event depends on the observer.This being said, I believe that you mostly illustrated the title.What I believe is a flaw here is the lack of a certain mathematical/geometrical meaning to your image: the cropping of the beautiful head of the swan seems random, more cropping might have had more impact or the entire graceful curve would have made it even better. There are more variables such as the grey triangle on the upper left corner, the indecisive composition.6', '2013-10-16 19:48:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116709, 1087152, 124982, '<td valign="top">It took me a second or two to figure out what I was looking at, but when it clicked, I was like "Crap, this is awesome!". Very creatively done, indeed! Love the footprints, and the blood is so life-like (a little disturbing!). Top 3 for me!</td>', 'It took me a second or two to figure out what I was looking at, but when it clicked, I was like "Crap, this is awesome!". Very creatively done, indeed! Love the footprints, and the blood is so life-like (a little disturbing!). Top 3 for me!', '2013-10-16 19:49:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116710, 1087187, 124815, '<td valign="top">The processing, quite heavy, works here on the account of the subject (ashes, sand)<br/>A good image<br/>6 (for now)</td>', 'The processing, quite heavy, works here on the account of the subject (ashes, sand)A good image6 (for now)', '2013-10-16 19:50:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116711, 1087121, 124982, '<td valign="top">It does take courage to be out in that weather! Great shot for the book. Wish it was a little more processed (more contrast and perhaps more dark/ominous water and sky -- my preference). But still top 10 for me!</td>', 'It does take courage to be out in that weather! Great shot for the book. Wish it was a little more processed (more contrast and perhaps more dark/ominous water and sky -- my preference). But still top 10 for me!', '2013-10-16 19:50:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116712, 1086157, 124982, '<td valign="top">A beautiful scene, and most appropriate for the chosen book! Love colors and saturation, and I love the motion blur. I am not a big fan of the excessive border and what looks to be tonemapping, though. Still Top 10 for me.</td>', 'A beautiful scene, and most appropriate for the chosen book! Love colors and saturation, and I love the motion blur. I am not a big fan of the excessive border and what looks to be tonemapping, though. Still Top 10 for me.', '2013-10-16 19:51:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7116713, 1086865, 124982, '<td valign="top">Such a beautiful and stark image. Love the reflection and the subtle use of foreground.</td>', 'Such a beautiful and stark image. Love the reflection and the subtle use of foreground.', '2013-10-16 19:52:37.000000', NULL, 1),
